  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through Saturday)\nIssued at 344 PM CDT SUN SEP 20 2026\n\nOur upper ridge of late is situated from WRN TN SWWD to Mexico.\nIt is continuing to deteriorate as a closed low over Florida\npushes westward toward the Northern Gulf Coast. At the same time,\nan upper shortwave will move EWD out of the Rockies and toward\nthe Great Lakes late by Tuesday. Low to moderate chances for\ndiurnally enhanced convection will continue daily through\nTuesday. Some storms may be strong to severe at times, especially\non Monday and Tuesday with the main threat of strong downburst\nwinds. On Tuesday, guidance weakens/deteriorates the upper low\nover the coast. However, rain chances continue for Tuesday, but\ninstead will be focusing on activity ahead of a cold front that\nshould move through the area by Wednesday. Guidance has become\nfavorable with a pattern shift taking this front through the area\nand bringing much welcome more \"normal\" temperature readings for\nthis time of year into Central Alabama for the latter half of the\nweek and into next weekend. We may even see a few 50s in our\nnorthern counties.\n\n08",
